# name, type, stack, best use, strengths, tradeoffs, adoption note, docs, secondary source
rows = [
['Ant Design','Styled system','React','Feature-rich business applications, administration, complex forms and CRUD workflows.','Broad component catalog; consistent form and table patterns; tokens and an extensive companion ecosystem.','A recognizable visual language; advanced patterns can introduce several companion packages and more configuration.','Distinguish antd from ProComponents, the Ant Design Pro starter, Ant Design Charts and Ant Design X. “Pro” does not by itself mean a paid edition.','https://ant.design/docs/react/introduce/','https://github.com/ant-design/pro-components'],
['Atlassian Design System','Styled system','React / Atlaskit','Products integrated with Atlassian and collaboration interfaces with similar interaction needs.','Detailed foundations, content guidance and collaboration-oriented components.','Design-system licensing is tied to Atlassian integrations; package and asset permissions require careful separation.','ADS terms include an open-source carveout. Check each exact package license; neither a blanket prohibition nor blanket permission for all Atlaskit assets is accurate.','https://atlassian.design/','https://atlassian.design/license/'],
['Base UI','Headless foundation','React','A custom visual identity backed by composable interaction primitives.','Unstyled components; open composition; accessibility-focused behavior; freedom to choose a CSS approach.','You must supply visual design, tokens, layouts and larger application patterns; it is not an enterprise application suite.','Compare the actual controls and composition model with Radix and React Aria. Base UI is distinct from Material UI despite shared origins.','https://base-ui.com/react/overview/about','https://base-ui.com/react/overview/accessibility'],
['IBM Carbon','Styled system','React; other implementations vary','Enterprise platforms that need a disciplined visual language and consistent data presentation.','Extensive design guidance, tokens, UI shell and data-table patterns; a separate Carbon Charts ecosystem.','The IBM visual character is strong; richer product workflows may need companion packages or application composition.','Separate core Carbon, Carbon Charts and IBM Products components when checking coverage and compatibility. Not every package has the same lifecycle.','https://www.carbondesignsystem.com/','https://www.carbondesignsystem.com/building-blocks/data-visualization/overview'],
['Clarity','Styled system','Angular / CSS','Angular-based management consoles and structured enterprise administration.','Enterprise interaction guidance; data-oriented Angular components; coordinated visual styles and icons.','The active Angular offering is a different adoption path from the old framework-neutral Core package.','Clarity Core’s Web Components repository is archived. Do not treat old React/Vue examples as evidence of an actively maintained equivalent to Clarity Angular.','https://clarity.design/','https://github.com/vmware-clarity/core'],
['Cloudscape','Styled system','React','Resource management, operations consoles and workflows combining collections, detail views and guided tasks.','Integrated layouts, property filters, tables, split panels, wizards and detailed usage patterns.','Opinionated console structure; a distinct visual character; current chart wrappers introduce a separate Highcharts dependency.','The UI is not limited to AWS-backed products. Core open-source licensing does not remove the need to check Highcharts terms when using the new charts.','https://cloudscape.design/','https://cloudscape.design/components/charts/'],
['Fluent 2','Styled system','React web; platform-specific libraries','Productivity tools, collaboration apps and experiences seeking a Microsoft-familiar visual language.','Cross-platform design guidance, tokens, themes and well-developed interaction patterns.','Web, native and older Fluent implementations are not interchangeable; verify component and token parity for your platform.','Choose the intended Fluent generation and implementation explicitly. Microsoft ecosystem familiarity is a benefit, not a requirement to use Microsoft backend services.','https://fluent2.microsoft.design/','https://react.fluentui.dev/'],
['FlyonUI','Tailwind toolkit','Tailwind CSS + JavaScript','Fast Tailwind-based interfaces where prebuilt styling and markup are useful.','Semantic component classes, themes and a broad set of interface elements and integrations.','JavaScript initialization and framework lifecycles need integration work; complex widgets may depend on third-party plugins.','The original code is MIT, but the current license page also describes bundled Preline dual-license terms. Review those terms and any paid templates separately.','https://flyonui.com/docs/getting-started/quick-start/','https://flyonui.com/docs/getting-started/license/'],
['Material UI','Styled system','React','General-purpose web applications that benefit from familiar Material components and a large React ecosystem.','Broad styled component coverage, theming, documentation and optional MUI X grids, pickers and charts.','Material styling may need deliberate adaptation; advanced MUI X features can require commercial licenses.','Material UI and MUI X are separate product layers. Compare Community, Pro and Premium against required features; do not infer full grid capability from the free core library.','https://mui.com/material-ui/getting-started/','https://mui.com/x/introduction/licensing/'],
['PatternFly','Styled system','React / HTML-CSS','Infrastructure, developer tools and operational administration with dense, task-focused workflows.','Console-oriented patterns, data views, wizards and extensions for specialist operational experiences.','Its operations aesthetic may be less natural for consumer or brand-led products; extensions add their own integration surface.','Inventory core components and extensions separately. Red Hat origins do not restrict it to Red Hat products or infrastructure.','https://www.patternfly.org/','https://www.patternfly.org/components/all-components/'],
['Primer','Styled system','React; Rails / CSS ecosystem','Developer-facing tools, repositories, collaboration and structured content workflows.','GitHub-familiar interaction language, tokens, Octicons and product patterns for search, navigation and editing.','A recognizable developer-tool aesthetic; some documented shared components are internal rather than general public APIs.','Distinguish Product UI from Brand UI, and check the status and public availability of each component before planning around it.','https://primer.style/','https://primer.style/product/components/'],
['Radix Primitives','Headless foundation','React','Teams building a bespoke design system or adding accessible controls incrementally.','Unstyled, granular primitives; focus and keyboard behavior; flexible composition and styling.','Visual design, higher-level workflows, data grids and charting remain your responsibility.','Radix Primitives and Radix Themes are different offerings. A styled documentation example does not mean Primitives ships that appearance.','https://www.radix-ui.com/primitives/docs/overview/introduction','https://www.radix-ui.com/primitives/docs/overview/accessibility'],
['React Aria Components','Headless foundation','React','Custom interfaces where accessibility, internationalization and complex input behavior are central.','Style-free components, adaptive interactions, keyboard behavior and internationalization support.','Requires a visual system and application-level composition; the styling and state APIs need team familiarity.','React Aria Components is the unstyled component layer. It is distinct from the lower-level hooks and the styled React Spectrum system.','https://react-aria.adobe.com/','https://react-aria.adobe.com/getting-started'],
['React Spectrum','Styled system','React','Accessible, adaptive web applications comfortable with Adobe’s Spectrum visual language.','Coordinated styled components, light/dark modes, adaptive input behavior and internationalization.','The Spectrum identity is a deliberate constraint; bespoke brand expression may be easier with an unstyled foundation.','Choose Spectrum for the styled system and React Aria for visual freedom. They share an ecosystem but solve different adoption needs.','https://react-spectrum.adobe.com/','https://react-spectrum.adobe.com/react-spectrum/index.html'],
['Salt','Styled system','React','Dense analytical workspaces, professional tools and interfaces needing adjustable information density.','Density controls, theme tokens and components developed for demanding enterprise workflows.','Specialist grids and charts can involve external integrations; experimental lab components have a different stability level.','Inspect core versus lab status. Salt themes for AG Grid or Highcharts do not confer licenses for those products; verify fonts and assets for the chosen theme.','https://www.saltdesignsystem.com/salt/index','https://www.saltdesignsystem.com/salt/getting-started/developing'],
['SAP UI5 family','Styled system','OpenUI5 / SAPUI5; Web Components','Business applications aligned with SAP Fiori, especially alongside an existing SAP landscape.','Enterprise controls, internationalization, themes and compact/cozy density; Web Components can cross framework boundaries.','A family of technologies rather than one interchangeable library; framework and licensing choices affect integration.','Choose among OpenUI5, SAPUI5 and UI5 Web Components explicitly. Open-source Web Components are framework-neutral; SAPUI5 distribution and entitlement are separate questions.','https://ui5.github.io/webcomponents/','https://sdk.openui5.org/'],
['shadcn/ui','Owned-source approach','React + Tailwind CSS','Brand-led products and teams that want direct ownership of component source.','Editable source, composable components, blocks and a registry-based distribution model.','Your team owns consistency, local changes and upstream update reconciliation; copying components is not a maintenance strategy.','Treat it as a way to build your component library. Establish ownership, review and upgrade conventions; track which underlying primitives and dependencies each component uses.','https://ui.shadcn.com/docs','https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components']
]

def esc(s): return html.escape(s, quote=True)
def ident(s): return ''.join(c.lower() if c.isalnum() else '-' for c in s).strip('-')
data=[]
for r in rows:
    d=dict(zip(['name','kind','stack','fit','pros','cons','note','docs','extra'],r));d['id']=ident(d['name']);data.append(d)
(ROOT/'guide-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2))
